# Local, competition-specific data -- never commit this.
# The whole point of the toolkit is that the repo stays generic/public
# and everything environment-specific lives only on the machine you run it from.
config/answers.local.psd1
logs/
*.local.psd1
*.zip

# Pre-staged third-party binaries (Sysmon, Splunk UF, ...) -- large, and
# not something to redistribute through this repo regardless of size;
# download them yourself per docs/PREP-SHEET.md and stage them here.
# Our own prep-time helper scripts live in prep/, not here, precisely so
# they don't disappear into this rule.
tools/

# Past injects, team packets and other competition paperwork. Useful to
# read and to practise against, not ours to republish -- and a public repo
# is the wrong place for it regardless. Keep it local; your coach decides
# if any of it gets shared.
injects-archive/

# Raw Discord export, same reasoning as injects-archive/ above -- useful
# to mine for ground truth, not ours to republish, and almost certainly
# contains other people's messages. Keep it local.
discord-archive/

# The practice lab. This is OUR test environment -- Hyper-V VM building,
# unattended-install answer files, ISO staging, VM screenshots, unsticking
# wedged VMs. NONE of it ever runs on a competition box, and none of it is
# part of what the toolkit does on game day. It also describes the shape of
# our own practice setup, which is nobody else's business. Keep it local.
lab/

# These test the lab kit and import from lab\, so they cannot live in a
# repo that does not ship lab\ -- a fresh clone would fail to even load
# them. The toolkit's own tests (modules, logic, UI, repo policy) stay.
tests/Lab.Tests.ps1
tests/LabHost.Tests.ps1
tests/LabGuest.Tests.ps1
.aider*
